# Search-tool ignore file — ripgrep honours this, so Claude Code's Grep does too.
#
# NOTE: Glob does NOT honour this file (verified 2026-07-26: `Glob("**/*.py")`
# still returns 500 matches, ~70% of them worktree copies). Keep scoping Glob
# patterns by hand, e.g. Glob("swingbot/**/*.py"). Only Grep is fixed here.
#
# Why this file exists: at repo root, `Grep("def sector_heat")` used to TIME OUT
# after 20s and return nothing, because ripgrep was walking ~2,600 files / 160 MB
# of caches, logs and three full worktree copies of the repo. It now answers
# instantly. `Glob("**/*.py")` returns 500 matches for 232 real .py files.
#
# This is deliberately separate from .gitignore: .gitignore controls what git
# tracks, this controls what code search walks. Some paths below are tracked or
# untracked-but-wanted; they just must never be searched.
#
# To search these anyway, pass an explicit path: Grep(path="market_data/...").

# Three full copies of this repo. Searching them points you at the wrong branch.
.claude/worktrees/

# OHLCV caches — 521 symbol dirs / 91 MB and 77 flat CSVs. Never grepped for code.
market_data/
data/backtest_cache/

# Runtime JSON state + rotated logs.
data/
logs/
exports/

# SDD execution ledger: 130+ review diffs (largest 174 KB) and a 173 KB
# progress.md. Read progress.md by tail, never by search.
.superpowers/sdd/*.diff
.superpowers/sdd/*.log

__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# The SPA's dependency tree: ~1,100 packages. Grepping for a TS symbol at
# repo root without this walks all of it and finds Angular's own sources
# before yours. `frontend/src/` is deliberately still searchable.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.angular/
